    "transcription": "Each analysis is one sheet of the named Supplementary Data file, copied unchanged with openpyxl 3.1.5: 'FRET E' to fret_e, 'kinetic model' to rates_s_inv, the two 'uncertainty rates' blocks to uncertainty_plus and uncertainty_minus. Rows are the start state and columns the end state, in s^-1, in the state order the lab submitted (Supplementary Data 4). For Fig. 5 only the sheets whose name ends in _FS_2 (two FRET states) are copied, the models the paper's Fig. 5 compares; the other models are in Supplementary Tables 2-4. Each file's SHA-256 is that of its manifest entry (published.data), and each equals the same table in the paper's Source Data archive."
